Z||000003||mrfiero||01-17-2001||10:29 PM||||Check your rear links.  Over time the bushings get distorted and don't do their job as effectively as they should.  The passenger side adjustable link bushings are the worst offenders......they nearly get squeezed out.<P>I would take the links off and inspect the bushings.||||reg||1
Z||000004||G-Nasty||01-17-2001||10:48 PM||||I have the same problem on one of my GT's. It is the strut tower bracket support plates above your struts. If you have ever had someone replace the struts...they probably removed these and just used the thin supports. I had struts put in and the idiot ASE mechanics kept the support 1/4" thick support plates. The rear feels like jello.||||reg||1
